				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				105,
				2
			],
			"Message": "docs(Rest): Redefine Rest as JS bundler CLI, not HTTP server\n\nThe README and Architecture.md documents still described Rest as an HTTP/REST\ncompilation API server with dual OXC/SWC backends, but the project was refactored\ninto a build-time CLI/library that compiles the Dependency/Editor VS Code source\ntree via a single OXC-backed pipeline.\n\nRepurpose all documentation to reflect the current architecture:\n\n- Correct the tagline, overview, and inline descriptions from \"HTTP/REST server\"\n  to \"JS bundler / CLI compilation pipeline\"\n- Replace the consumption model from \"Maintain/Cocoon make HTTP requests\" to\n  \"Maintain invokes the CLI, bundles are written to Output, Cocoon loads them via\n  require()\"\n- Clarify that SWC is a legacy module name whose Compile.rs now runs the OXC\n  pipeline; ESBuild is an optional subprocess fallback\n- Update Rust minimum to 1.95.0 / Edition 2024\n- Add missing dependencies (walkdir, globset) and new sections (License,\n  Changelog, project maintainers)\n- Normalize emoji spacing to HTML entities and collapse multi-line table cells\n  to single-line markup\n- Refresh the architecture diagram and all data-flow connection tables\n\nNo functional code changes — documentation only.",
			"SHA": "f987c897ca7802afad6ebad889e5f90dfb22f30c"
		},
